import object_detector

# Parameters for detection
labels=['white dining table','white dining table', 'blue modern tv stand', 'blue modern tv stand']

# Create an instance object of the object detector
detector = object_detector.Object_Detector_Tool()

# Execute the detection
result = detector.execute(image='image_path', labels=labels, save_object=True, saved_image_path='detected_objects')

# Get the detected objects
detected_objects = result[0]['detected_objects']
object_number = result[1]['object_number']

# Create a dictionary with the detected objects and their positions
result_dict = {
    'detected_objects': detected_objects,
    'object_number': object_number
}

print(result_dict)
```

This code takes the image path as a parameter when executing the object detection tool. It also includes all the necessary parameters, except for the object labels, which is a list provided with the tool input. After detecting the objects, it creates a dictionary that maps each detected object with its position in the image. Finally, it prints the dictionary that includes the detected objects and their positions, including object number.
